[0.026,"o","\u001b[H\u001b[38;5;174m ▐\u001b[48;5;16m▛███▛█\u001b[12G\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[1mClaude Code\u001b[24G\u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;246mv2.1.325\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;174m▝▜\u001b[48;5;16m█\u001b[7G█\u001b[49m█▀\u001b[12G\u001b[38;5;246mdeepseek-flash[\u001b[28Gm] · API Usage Billing\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;174m ▝▝   ▝▝ \u001b[12G\u001b[38;5;246m/work\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[48;5;237m\u001b[38;5;246m❯ \u001b[38;5;231mPlease implement this issue.\u001b[39m                                                            \r\u001b[1B                              \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m#66 Which invoices are overdue\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m                              \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231mThe aging report tells me how much is overdue, but not which invoices, so I end up \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bsearch\u001b[13Gthe JSON file. Add \u001b[38;5;153m--details\u001b[38;5;231m to \u001b[38;5;153minvoicer aging\u001b[38;5;231m.\u001b[39m                          \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B                                                         \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231mAcceptance criteria:\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m                    \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m1. With \u001b[38;5;153m--details\u001b[38;5;231m, each bucket's row is followed by its invoices, one per line: the \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Binvo\u001b[8Gce's id, the customer's name, the due dat\u001b[50G,\u001b[52Gthe days overdue\u001b[69Ga\u001b[71Gd\u001b[73Gthe\u001b[77Gamount.\u001b[39m   \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m2. W\u001b[8Gthin\u001b[13Ga buck\u001b[20Gt, the invoice overdue the longest come\u001b[61Gfirst.\u001b[39m                 \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m3\u001b[6GThe amounts are the invoices' totals, printed as\u001b[55Gthe repo\u001b[64Gt prints amounts, and they\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Badd up\u001b[10Gto the bucke\u001b[23G's\u001b[26Gamount.\u001b[39m                                                         \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m4. Without \u001b[38;5;153m--details\u001b[38;5;231m, \u001b[38;5;153minvoicer aging\u001b[38;5;231m prints exactly what it prints today.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mI'll\u001b[8Gstart\u001b[14Gby\u001b[17Gexploring\u001b[27Gthe\u001b[31Gcodebase\u001b[40Gto\u001b[43Gunderstand\u001b[54Gthe\u001b[58Gexisting\u001b[67Gaging\u001b[73Greport.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mInspecting\u001b[14Gdata,\u001b[20GREADME,\u001b[28Grunning\u001b[36Gtests\u001b[42Gand\u001b[46Gaging\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m  ⎿  $ head -c 3000 /work/data/invoices.json; echo; echo \"---\"; cat /work/README.md; echo \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;5;246m\"---\"; npm test 2>&1 | tail -20; echo \"---\"; npm \u001b[56Gun d\u001b[61Gv -- aging data/invoices.json \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B--today 2026-11-15\u001b[39m\u001b[34;1H\u001b[32;3H"]
